  "rationale": "structural: `requirements.cli.requirements_review_skill.commit.check` says only that, before the commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill \"MUST direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text.\" That clause constrains what the skill's text tells agents. It names no library, algorithm, signature, type, field or delegation to a named interface.\n\nI tested the clause against an alternative. Take a skill that gives the same direction in different words, in a different section or in a different order. It still satisfies the clause. Any rewrite that drops the direction violates it, but that is a gap in content, not in how the skill is built. So every clause specifies observable content only, and no structural obligation needs implementation evidence.\n\nThe review root `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` is the artifact that carries that content. The outline I could read showed only elided sections (`Workflow`, `Choosing references` and others), so I did not verify the skill's wording. I submit Success because no structural obligation exists here and no root is missing.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one observable obligation. Before the commit, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to check that the book holds exactly the agreed text. The skill is static text, so the test is a content assertion on it.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_checks_the_book_holds_exactly_the_agreed_text]` carries `{test}`. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)`. That reads `bundled_skill(\"habeas-requirements\")`, which is `SKILL.md` plus its references with whitespace collapsed. `assert_text` then asserts `contains` for the phrase \"Check with `git diff` that the book holds exactly the agreed text, then commit it\".\n\nThe phrase covers both the check (`git diff`, the book holds exactly the agreed text) and its place before the commit (\"then commit it\"). If the skill dropped the instruction, or changed what it checks, the assertion would fail.\n\nThe actual skill text, in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md` Workflow step 5, contains this sentence. It is the same phrase after whitespace collapse. No other input class or boundary affects the obligation.",
